# The FORTRAN reference is read-only

`meradgen-fortran/` is an unmodified extraction of the upstream
`meradgen10.tar`. It has been verified byte-identical to that tarball. Its
value is entirely in being untouched: it is the definition of correct output
for the whole project.

## Never

- Edit any file under `meradgen-fortran/`, including comments and whitespace.
- Add `print`, `write`, or debug output to produce a trace.
- Apply a bug fix here, even an obviously correct one.
- Reformat, modernise, or convert to free-form.

## Instead

To instrument the reference, copy it — never edit `meradgen-fortran/`:

```bash
python3 comparison-autoreport/harness/inject_rand4.py \
  --src meradgen-fortran \
  --dst /tmp/meradgen-fortran-rand4
```

The parity CMake does this into the build tree automatically. A throwaway
inject into `/tmp` is fine for one-off patches.

If a genuine upstream bug is found, record it in `WORK_NOTES_STATUS.md` /
`WORK_NOTES_MERADGEN_TYPOS.md` with the file and line. Do not fix it in
the reference — the parity tree must reproduce it until a decision says
otherwise. Production may correct selected typos.

## Verifying integrity

```bash
mkdir -p /tmp/mg && tar -xf meradgen10.tar -C /tmp/mg
diff -r --exclude=meradgen10.tar /tmp/mg meradgen-fortran
```

This must report no differences. If it does not, the reference has been
corrupted and should be restored from the tarball before any comparison work.
